  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-4000004795</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-year financing support Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative (EITI) International Secretariat (2021-2024)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The subsidy for 2021-2014 concerns a general contribution to the EITI with non-earmarked spending by the organization&#x2019;s International Secretariat. The contribution is used for activities related to the implementation of the EITI Standard. This focuses on requirements to EITI member states that promote transparency between companies and government agencies regarding financial flows, licensing, ownership of companies etc.. A formalized relationship between governments, companies and civil society organizations is instrumental in this. This form is quite unique, certainly for the traditionally conservative raw materials sectors. Implementation of the Standard takes place in EITI member states in this context by means of &apos;multi-stakeholder&apos; groups. The Dutch contribution can also be used for assistance by the International Secretariat to these processes. The Netherlands is one of a number of developed countries (e.g. France, Germany, Switzerland, the US, Canada etc.) that support the organization financially. The Netherlands is thus both a &apos;supporting country&apos; (by means of this contribution) of the EITI, as well as an &apos;implementing country&apos;, as we also implement the EITI Standard ourselves.</narrative>
  </description>
